dux-mono-regular.woff2 and dux-mono-bold.woff2 are Roboto Mono Regular and
Bold (weights 400 and 700, instanced from the variable font), from
googlefonts/robotomono, tag v3.001
(https://github.com/googlefonts/robotomono), file
fonts/variable/RobotoMono[wght].ttf. Licensed OFL-1.1.

dux-mono-symbols.woff2 is a subset of JetBrains Mono Nerd Font Mono Regular,
from ryanoasis/nerd-fonts release v3.5.0
(https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts), cut to the structural glyph
ranges dux needs to draw TUI-shaped output: arrows (U+2190-21FF),
miscellaneous technical (U+2300-23FF), box drawing and block elements
(U+2500-25FF), miscellaneous symbols and dingbats (U+2600-27BF), braille
patterns (U+2800-28FF), and the Powerline private-use glyphs
(U+E0A0-E0D7). Licensed OFL-1.1.

Neither upstream OFL.txt file declares a Reserved Font Name after its
copyright statement, so OFL clause 3 does not, on its own, require either
of these files to be renamed. Every file bundled here is renamed anyway, as
a precaution: each is either instanced (Roboto Mono) or subset (the
JetBrains Mono Nerd Font Mono cut), which OFL treats as a Modified Version,
and renaming avoids any appearance that a modified, subsetted build is the
certified upstream font. Each file's name table (IDs 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 16, 17)
was rewritten to a family dux owns instead: the two Roboto Mono weights
become "Dux Mono" (Regular / Bold), and the JetBrains subset becomes
"Dux Mono Symbols".

Reproduction, from the exact upstream files named above:

  # Roboto Mono: instance the variable font at wght=400 and wght=700,
  # then rename the family in each instanced TTF's name table (fontTools
  # ttLib, IDs 1/2/3/4/6/16/17 -> "Dux Mono" / "Regular" or "Bold"),
  # then compress each to woff2 (fontTools ttLib, flavor="woff2").
  fonttools varLib.instancer RobotoMono[wght].ttf wght=400 -o RobotoMono-Regular.ttf
  fonttools varLib.instancer RobotoMono[wght].ttf wght=700 -o RobotoMono-Bold.ttf
  # (rename + woff2 compress as described above)

  # JetBrains Mono Nerd Font Mono: subset to the structural unicode ranges,
  # rename the family to "Dux Mono Symbols", then compress to woff2.
  pyftsubset JetBrainsMonoNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf \
    --unicodes="U+2190-21FF,U+2300-23FF,U+2500-25FF,U+2600-27BF,U+2800-28FF,U+E0A0-E0D7" \
    --output-file=symbols-subset.ttf \
    --glyph-names --symbol-cmap --legacy-cmap --notdef-glyph --notdef-outline \
    --recommended-glyphs --name-IDs='*' --name-legacy --name-languages='*'
  # (rename + woff2 compress as described above)

